course: dictionary
lesson: 2758
title: Followers and learners
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A disciple is a follower who learns from a teacher or leader and believes in their ideas. In the Bible, the disciples were the people who followed Jesus and learned from him. The word is about learning from someone, not just knowing them.
explain: Look for clues. «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.» The word first tells you these were the earliest followers. The twelve closest were also called apostles, so every apostle was a disciple, but not every disciple was an apostle.
explain: Read the words around it. «The risen Jesus met his friends: Mary Magdalene in the garden, two sad disciples on the road to Emmaus, doubting Thomas, and Peter by the lake...» The list of names shows that disciples were people who followed Jesus closely. Outside religion, a disciple can be someone who copies a famous coach or artist.
fact: A disciple is a follower who learns from a teacher or leader.
fact: The twelve closest followers of Jesus were also called apostles.
fact: «Pentecostal churches are named after Pentecost, when the Holy Spirit came on the first disciples.»
fact: Outside religion, a famous coach or artist can have disciples who copy their ways.
fact: Useful phrases: the twelve disciples, a disciple of someone, call disciples.
exercise: In the Bible, what is a disciple? | A servant who cooks the meals | A king who rules a country | *A follower who learns from Jesus | A stranger who never met Jesus
exercise: «Christianity grew out of Judaism: Jesus, Mary and the first disciples were Jewish.» Find and copy one word that means followers who learn from a teacher. | Hebrew | Judaism | Christianity | *disciples
exercise: A famous coach has many disciples. What does this suggest? | People who are always late for training | People who sell the coach's shoes | *People who copy the coach's ways and learn from them | People who sleep in the coach's house
test: The risen Jesus met «two sad disciples on the road to Emmaus». What does disciples mean here? | Travellers who had never heard of Jesus | *Followers who had learned from Jesus | People who sell bread on the road | Soldiers marching to a war
test: What is the difference between a disciple and an apostle? | They are two kinds of animal | Apostles are a type of church building | A disciple is always one of the twelve closest followers | *An apostle was one of the twelve closest followers, while a disciple can be any follower
exam: What is a disciple? | A servant who works in a palace | A teacher who never has any students | A fish caught in a net | *A follower who learns from a teacher or leader and believes in their ideas
